# Docker build context for the `cuda` image (repo-root Dockerfile).
# The Dockerfile COPYs only: pyproject.toml, uv.lock, submodules/, core/, and the
# pyproject.toml manifests of the other workspace members. Everything else is excluded
# here — without this file the context is the entire repo (100+ GB: runs/, data/,
# output/, .venv/, ...), which turned `ensure_image`'s automatic rebuild into a
# multi-hour silent block (T26 follow-up, 2026-10-09).

# VCS / environments / caches
.git
.gitmodules
.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache

# Data, outputs, run registry — never needed at image-build time
data/
output/
runs/
assets/
results_visual/
reviews/
docs/
papers/
scratch/
weights/
test_tmp/
.claude_notes/
.devcontainer/
LLFF/
viseron/

# Large media / archives anywhere
*.zip
*.mp4
*.jpg
*.pdf

# Workspace members: the Dockerfile COPYs only each member's pyproject.toml
# (sources are bind-mounted at runtime from /workspace), so exclude the member
# trees and re-include just the manifests.
motion-seg/*
!motion-seg/pyproject.toml
omniverse-pipeline/*
!omniverse-pipeline/pyproject.toml
amp-ui/*
!amp-ui/pyproject.toml
orchestrator/*
!orchestrator/pyproject.toml
scene-gen/*
!scene-gen/pyproject.toml
camera_sync/*
!camera_sync/sync_display/pyproject.toml
!camera_sync/recorder/pyproject.toml
!camera_sync/sync_analyzer/pyproject.toml
!camera_sync/rtsp_capture/pyproject.toml

# Inside submodules/ the CUDA extension sources ARE the build input — exclude only
# the MultiBodySync checkpoint blobs (downloaded separately per WINDOWS_SETUP.md §7).
submodules/multibody-sync-4dgs/ckpt/
